# Line endings are repo state, not a per-developer git setting.
#
# Without this file, whether a checkout gets LF or CRLF depends on each
# clone's core.autocrlf, so a file written on Windows and a file written on
# Linux can differ by bytes alone. That divergence is invisible in a normal
# diff and breaks anything that compares committed bytes.
#
# Everything tracked here is text (Python, Markdown, TOML, YAML, INI, the
# Dockerfile, the Alembic templates); there are no binary files in this repo,
# so there is nothing to exempt. If a binary artifact is ever added, give it an
# explicit `binary` line below -- otherwise the `text` attribute will strip
# CR bytes out of it on commit and silently corrupt it.
* text eol=lf
